The bug: `pos = int((cut / cell_length) * (len(text) - 1))` — an approximation of the split position. This can be wrong. E.g., text with wide chars. The issue in textual #4996. Let me think about what the actual fix was in rich. The actual fix (rich PR #3237? "fix split cells") — Let me recall. Rich commit: "fix Segment._split_cells" — CHANGELOG entry. Let me check CHANGELOG for hints.

Actually the known fix: the initial pos estimate can overshoot; the loop only moves forward. If pos estimate is beyond the actual cut position, the split is wrong. Fix: compute pos properly, e.g., iterate from 0 or use a better estimate and handle backwards.

